  'Juvenile Justice explains why the juvenile court was created, how its rehabilitative mission has changed, and why youth justice sits between welfare, punishment, public safety, and children''s rights. Students study adolescent development and delinquency theory, statutory system flow, police and school decision points, diversion and restorative pathways, due process after In re Gault, detention and risk assessment, adjudication and disposition, transfer to adult court, confinement and reentry, disparities, crossover youth, community safety, evidence and policy analysis, and reform strategy.',
