"4d59592a-f5b2-4ce4-80b0-7e342264cdd6", "type": "concept", "title": "Developmental reform, decarceration, evidence-based practice, and racial justice movements"}, {"id": "c0666b88-3697-4de8-be94-03593aaaec11", "type": "concept", "title": "Local, state, tribal, and federal variation"}], "description": "The gist is to see youth justice as historically unstable."}, {"id": "4767bb93-f0dc-4947-984d-9bb982cfdde6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core values", "children": [{"id": "716b2b08-3bf5-4b6d-93f1-e0197a2b5154", "type": "concept", "title": "Public safety, accountability, rehabilitation, proportionality, due process, dignity, family integrity, and community repair"}, {"id": "71185552-07b0-45ee-8d70-a322550dd4f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Best interests of the child versus community protection"}, {"id": "fa38083f-9251-425c-b170-9c6840da2896", "type": "concept", "title": "Youth voice and participation"}], "description": "Students identify the values that compete in youth justice."}]}, {"id": "170886c9-7cd2-4400-b8ce-1d01db020a69", "type": "topic", "title": "Adolescent Development, Delinquency Theories, and Youth Behavior in Context", "description": "This module grounds juvenile justice in developmental science and criminological theory so students can distinguish youthful risk-taking from adult culpability and chronic harm.", "children": [{"id": "e2927d24-1859-4fef-884e-5bb45dc8bc11", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Developmental science", "children": [{"id": "dff90e78-fb29-4b75-b253-ad84f7c67170", "type": "concept", "title": "Brain development, impulse control, reward sensitivity, peer influence, identity formation, and capacity for change"}, {"id": "1a71421d-7ef3-4281-8bcd-af1d9f92920a", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma, adverse childhood experiences, disability, and mental health"}, {"id": "a8cf561d-af2a-41aa-9a8b-d7837c6e785c", "type": "concept", "title": "Developmental differences from adults"}], "description": "Students learn why adolescence matters legally and practically."}, {"id": "5e2be6bd-240a-4134-b2dc-14b246efa516", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Delinquency theories", "children": [{"id": "b26897fb-12cb-44db-94a4-3aa39da1bdf8", "type": "concept", "title": "Social learning, strain, control, labeling, routine activities, life-course, and developmental theories"}, {"id": "a27e8016-e589-493c-970e-a02b21cb8a38", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk factors, protective factors, desistance, and resilience"}, {"id": "0e4cfaf4-9246-4092-95d3-32a1fda1bd2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Family, school, peer, neighborhood, and online contexts"}], "description": "The point is to connect behavior to social context and intervention."}, {"id": "daa25676-1e31-43c9-90e2-26f7965909b9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Youth behavior and culpability", "children": [{"id": "bf8b34de-a9d5-44ae-b093-87c202dbed15", "type": "concept", "title": "Status offenses, delinquency, serious violence, substance use, and group offending"}, {"id": "2a9b047e-ed3c-48c6-ab8e-e8dee4598097", "type": "concept", "title": "Maturity, intent, responsibility, and capacity for rehabilitation"}, {"id": "7730786e-f326-439d-9ed8-4cefcc639a16", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding deterministic or deficit-only thinking"}], "description": "Students practice applying theory to real cases."}]}, {"id": "208bf61d-f00c-4139-b65a-f3b8c14f582d", "type": "topic", "title": "Legal Framework: JJDPA, State Systems, Jurisdiction, Status Offenses, and System Flow", "description": "Students learn the statutory and institutional structure that moves youth from referral to intake, court, supervision, placement, or diversion.", "children": [{"id": "3e16f742-a747-4bb8-bc5f-b3bd2471d08f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Federal framework", "children": [{"id": "980950c2-7405-4dca-af13-aa3a11e91db5", "type": "concept", "title": "Juvenile Justice and Delinquency Prevention Act"}, {"id": "38a22d68-660f-443f-a742-38df18786568", "type": "concept", "title": "Deinstitutionalization of status offenders, sight-and-sound separation, jail removal, and racial and ethnic disparities"}, {"id": "71e7b044-a898-4d7a-94d0-8c49cb3cfe44", "type": "concept", "title": "OJJDP funding, state compliance, and data reporting"}], "description": "Students learn the national guardrails around state systems."}, {"id": "cbade92a-21eb-45fa-9c84-7dd3518d8375", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Jurisdiction and system flow", "children": [{"id": "97423dec-ba02-47b6-bf8e-e0311a0348e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Age boundaries, delinquency jurisdiction, status offense jurisdiction, dependency overlap, and tribal/state/federal issues"}, {"id": "70152d19-b251-449d-8a2e-4487a6fbabd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Referral, intake, detention screening, petition, adjudication, disposition, review, and aftercare"}, {"id": "652d484a-0359-423d-bac6-3eb023955b0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Informal adjustment and formal processing"}], "description": "The gist is to understand how youth enter and move through the system."}, {"id": "add0311b-1e9a-44d6-a471-9e6328429f71", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Status offenses", "children": [{"id": "a7588d4e-0ffe-4935-a44d-a002b3ab9474", "type": "concept", "title": "Truancy, running away, curfew violations, incorrigibility, and underage possession"}, {"id": "48d92e34-90e5-4802-b327-99e2c1900057", "type": "concept", "title": "Valid court order exception and detention risks"}, {"id": "3167c124-36e9-48cf-89a1-49c041938dc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Family conflict, school exclusion, homelessness, and service needs"}], "description": "Students analyze why noncriminal youth conduct is controversial."}]}, {"id": "08c5bb8a-8f13-41dd-bfb2-fc4d6e20156f", "type": "topic", "title": "Police-Youth Encounters, School Policing, and Front-End Decision Points", "description": "This topic examines the earliest and often most consequential choices in youth justice: contact, stop, questioning, arrest, referral, school discipline, and informal resolution.", "children": [{"id": "1ac69372-9076-424c-930d-e6cd9068de82", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Police-youth contact", "children": [{"id": "1966ae9f-ea37-4b93-8a09-4b753b212ce6", "type": "concept", "title": "Stops, searches, questioning, arrest, citations, field release, and referral"}, {"id": "eee043f4-15a8-4c66-847c-19a8c4cf705b", "type": "concept", "title": "Developmentally appropriate communication and Miranda comprehension"}, {"id": "652e29b6-fbe3-460c-a9cc-4b9d43654449", "type": "concept", "title": "Use of force, de-escalation, and procedural justice"}], "description": "Students learn how early encounters shape trust and case outcomes."}, {"id": "604f9982-a592-469c-8d2c-f8280bbe52b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "School-to-prison pipeline", "children": [{"id": "9ed20e2f-cc6f-4bc3-8936-95c937b269c0", "type": "concept", "title": "School resource officers, zero tolerance, exclusionary discipline, truancy, disorderly conduct, and referrals"}, {"id": "dcd7e4d6-d5f1-4d19-be4e-6d0de1ea24cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Race, disability, language status, and gender disparities"}, {"id": "bcbee7d6-b2c6-4bd9-acfd-f4471d8bf6d5", "type": "concept", "title": "School climate, restorative discipline, and threat assessment"}], "description": "The point is to understand how school discipline becomes court involvement."}, {"id": "7672c953-c491-4a72-8a23-b882e4a42e1d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Front-end discretion", "children": [{"id": "1da0a876-3146-4e62-a482-0d40fd3a1474", "type": "concept", "title": "Warning, station adjustment, family referral, crisis response, restorative referral, and community services"}, {"id": "5ed68b2c-d819-4cc0-916d-f2e29b751860", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation and bias safeguards"}, {"id": "e5a675fc-6ada-43ca-a3f6-503b77120a7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Youth and parent communication"}], "description": "Students identify decision points where diversion is possible."}]}, {"id": "a2577fb8-3a16-49d1-b0db-ec6d4302bc0e", "type": "topic", "title": "Intake, Diversion, Restorative Pathways, and Community-Based Alternatives", "description": "Students study how systems can respond to harm without formal adjudication, including diversion, restorative justice, services, and community-based accountability.", "children": [{"id": "8a8b3a69-0df9-4201-a42f-0704aa52114c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intake decision-making", "children": [{"id": "89e021e7-f803-4e5f-9594-687f66928468", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening, risk/needs assessment, legal sufficiency, victim input, family context, and service matching"}, {"id": "74123de7-c33c-44a9-a623-d17f0469c199", "type": "concept", "title": "Prosecutorial filing discretion and probation intake"}, {"id": "2c43020f-4922-4787-bf92-faa3884c0fc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity checks and net-widening risk"}], "description": "Students learn how formal processing can be avoided or triggered."}, {"id": "1fcfac9b-f11f-4d38-9d9e-f38acb7fac33", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diversion models", "children": [{"id": "4ccfb1c1-00dc-48ab-9b90-25156c293d22", "type": "concept", "title": "Informal adjustment, teen court, family group conferencing, restorative circles, community service, mentoring, and behavioral health referral"}, {"id": "de476590-0ac7-4842-9cc7-c0e7dc12c7a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility, consent, accountability, completion, and dismissal"}, {"id": "517c3aed-dafa-4b1e-af00-5b26d722aac4", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-risk youth and minimal intervention"}], "description": "The gist is to respond proportionately and constructively."}, {"id": "4a864f93-0bd0-4890-85e2-78f9b549c8f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Community-based alternatives", "children": [{"id": "69c66a2e-bafe-4c8e-b0c9-d10191f2daa5", "type": "concept", "title": "Multisystemic therapy, functional family therapy, cognitive behavioral interventions, mentoring, education support, and credible messengers"}, {"id": "10a09484-267f-4493-8fc5-56f609dcec8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Family engagement and culturally responsive practice"}, {"id": "4fde686f-1f8b-4b2f-b361-33d9f4d3a2d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Measuring success beyond recidivism"}], "description": "Students learn alternatives to custody and deep system involvement."}]}, {"id": "061e6541-32fd-4eb9-a23f-4085c7f886ec", "type": "topic", "title": "Juvenile Court Procedure, Due Process, Counsel, and Rights After In re Gault", "description": "This module teaches the core procedural rights of young people and the tension between informality, protection, and adversarial safeguards.", "children": [{"id": "5dbc0df1-dcfd-4ec4-8562-f205e0fe02a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gault and due process", "children": [{"id": "8fc592c8-af12-46d8-899c-27e1ca2140f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Notice, counsel, confrontation, cross-examination, privilege against self-incrimination, and proof standards"}, {"id": "c7e5527d-0234-44a7-9a3e-90e7bf13374a", "type": "concept", "title": "In re Gault, Winship, McKeiver, Breed, and related cases"}, {"id": "defdf853-c5c0-401b-bc91-a9200d077598", "type": "concept", "title": "Informality versus adversarial safeguards"}], "description": "Students learn the constitutional turn in juvenile court."}, {"id": "cadaadf7-7865-4bf5-880f-b9c179254021", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Youth defense", "children": [{"id": "baa8c166-6aef-4340-b812-bd76f30a68f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Client-directed representation, capacity, confidentiality, family involvement, immigration, education, disability, and collateral consequences"}, {"id": "9b632afa-c328-4ae2-bdfa-dc895a49e0b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Guardian ad litem versus defense counsel roles"}, {"id": "5cdda9ee-450c-4f6e-93ad-910bffaac8ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Effective assistance and caseload constraints"}], "description": "The point is to understand specialized representation for children."}, {"id": "8cfbfd16-1f21-46c1-b078-ef1c05329dbe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Courtroom practice", "children": [{"id": "3ff1c5c0-48a2-42d3-9857-0ddbd29a0343", "type": "concept", "title": "Petitions, detention hearings, adjudication, disposition, review hearings, probation violations, and appeals"}, {"id": "a539d745-c599-42d8-bb7c-a69bd7c74144", "type": "concept", "title": "Language access, competency, trauma-informed practice, and courtroom dignity"}, {"id": "f9bc537f-81b1-4a61-8353-f20453e865bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Records, confidentiality, and expungement"}], "description": "Students connect rights to procedure."}]}, {"id": "e42fa2c5-5e8b-4e6d-9bbb-0713dc3f0255", "type": "topic", "title": "Detention, Risk Assessment, Probation, and Pre-Adjudication Liberty", "description": "Students analyze when youth are detained before adjudication, how risk tools are used, and how pretrial decisions shape case outcomes and family stability.", "children": [{"id": "9473c63c-ce12-46b2-baae-08ba1157c8d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Detention decisions", "children": [{"id": "a8d7fc4e-b6db-4bd5-b7a5-2ac5b6213623", "type": "concept", "title": "Public safety, failure to appear, detention alternatives, home detention, electronic monitoring, and shelter care"}, {"id": "6972f08d-ff8c-4434-8993-734e72170c09", "type": "concept", "title": "Family disruption, school disruption, trauma, and case pressure"}, {"id": "38da11dd-eebc-4ff0-ab7c-3950a622d210", "type": "concept", "title": "Detention hearings and legal standards"}], "description": "Students learn the stakes of pre-adjudication confinement."}, {"id": "439ce779-142e-4940-9136-4aea8b66a83a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Risk and needs tools", "children": [{"id": "45cf018d-f307-4f49-af36-fea4ba7504b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Validation, bias, static and dynamic factors, overrides, transparency, and appeal"}, {"id": "1fa2f9e0-6fb7-4141-99d6-2b828c1c0ed8", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk principle and avoiding overintervention with low-risk youth"}, {"id": "2845d8e5-b040-48f5-a582-a05c90feb5c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Data quality and local calibration"}], "description": "The gist is to use tools cautiously and ethically."}, {"id": "911c9856-e881-464f-80e5-1104688f1bd9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Probation before adjudication", "children": [{"id": "8b332486-307b-47fa-91fe-c9c208bf2e88", "type": "concept", "title": "Informal supervision, conditions, drug testing, curfews, school attendance, and service referrals"}, {"id": "00116e28-faf7-4c2c-8412-e2df5e242c8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical violations and graduated responses"}, {"id": "1d9f120a-2abd-41b3-861b-23a39c4aae38", "type": "concept", "title": "Family support and youth voice"}], "description": "Students analyze supervision as both help and surveillance."}]}, {"id": "d2d98aa5-5606-4621-9af6-59696051cbde", "type": "topic", "title": "Adjudication, Disposition, Probation, Case Planning, and Graduated Responses", "description": "This topic follows a youth through findings, disposition, supervision, services, sanctions, incentives, and individualized case planning.", "children": [{"id": "f3a6d58b-e2a8-4706-b4a2-741196091bb9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Adjudication", "children": [{"id": "9a28ec54-0fcb-456f-baac-8d4398f53a7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Bench trials, evidence, witnesses, admissions, competency, and burdens of proof"}, {"id": "745241ce-6724-4804-99aa-60275d5c8838", "type": "concept", "title": "Negotiated admissions and plea-like processes"}, {"id": "80cb3d8c-82cf-407a-a8fb-9171c9db9377", "type": "concept", "title": "Collateral consequences of adjudication"}], "description": "Students learn how juvenile fact-finding differs from adult conviction."}, {"id": "9a31b3df-ca25-4c8b-a075-3620810cb018", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Disposition", "children": [{"id": "861acb13-5243-4b08-9023-17644b673aac", "type": "concept", "title": "Probation, restitution, community service, treatment, education, placement, and review"}, {"id": "ff09555f-e3dd-4c22-8308-19a25a9f0580", "type": "concept", "title": "Least restrictive alternative and individualized planning"}, {"id": "2afc43df-20d2-4da5-b75f-a2b232e2c689", "type": "concept", "title": "Family, victim, and community input"}], "description": "The point is to match response to youth, harm, and risk."}, {"id": "5895e994-f46c-4f7a-8e25-5c82891edb66", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Graduated responses", "children": [{"id": "897a6a39-1de6-4c12-abe7-bb5b2dd78009", "type": "concept", "title": "Incentives, sanctions, technical violations, responses to noncompliance, and positive youth development"}, {"id": "1a24c65c-de51-480f-8cf9-2ea21f1fecf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Case management, goal setting, and strengths-based practice"}, {"id": "86005b58-00ca-4c92-b349-dd61891b5fb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding violation-driven placement"}], "description": "Students study how supervision should respond to progress and setbacks."}]}, {"id": "c7963afd-9f0f-4e90-9c8f-32a248ff3f7e", "type": "topic", "title": "Transfer/Waiver to Adult Court, Developmental Culpability, and Supreme Court Doctrine", "description": "Students examine the highest-stakes jurisdictional decision in youth justice and the constitutional doctrine recognizing that children are different.", "children": [{"id": "9cd342ca-3979-4364-95cc-345c67362c8f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transfer mechanisms", "children": [{"id": "04366d9f-12b9-4e96-ac17-dba0b31e23c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Judicial waiver, prosecutorial direct file, statutory exclusion, reverse waiver, and blended sentencing"}, {"id": "eb55c7ad-9c8c-4e25-8c17-7d5f1c182820", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility, offense seriousness, age, record, amenability, and public safety"}, {"id": "eda86c65-94e9-49d2-8b3e-b6faa9f439ae", "type": "concept", "title": "State variation and reform efforts"}], "description": "Students learn how youth can be moved into adult court."}, {"id": "efcb0e5a-771c-4057-bdf8-bca4dbc3c418", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Developmental culpability", "children": [{"id": "cec9704a-9a24-4b34-af44-7e1c9010d3d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Roper, Graham, Miller, Montgomery, Jones, and proportionality"}, {"id": "6859b346-7467-49e3-9cd1-b09368ca763a", "type": "concept", "title": "Life without parole, death penalty limits, and sentencing mitigation"}, {"id": "85470051-6407-46ff-b1e7-ff628a9cd349", "type": "concept", "title": "Neuroscience, maturity, and capacity for change"}], "description": "The gist is to apply the principle that children are different."}, {"id": "b73e1bda-6716-4994-a1da-429153916950", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Adult-court consequences", "children": [{"id": "37e09780-85af-4f7e-b28e-f37b3bbaa741", "type": "concept", "title": "Adult jail/prison exposure, safety, education, records, collateral consequences, and recidivism"}, {"id": "3a84570e-f1f9-42ed-b127-7ae7765114f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Plea bargaining and trial rights"}, {"id": "fd4e5525-a5bb-4638-84c0-f3c1de8ab4d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial disparities and policy tradeoffs"}], "description": "Students analyze outcomes of adult prosecution."}]}, {"id": "53a0bf60-7e56-455a-8272-dae6b5bfe195", "type": "topic", "title": "Residential Placement, Conditions of Confinement, Reentry, and Aftercare", "description": "This module studies detention, residential treatment, correctional placement, education, health care, family contact, release planning, and reentry.", "children": [{"id": "bd48f51c-31dc-475d-8482-176728e2c2fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Placement continuum", "children": [{"id": "c67793b2-6db4-44e6-96ee-5bd8d71a1b5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Detention, residential treatment, group homes, secure facilities, wilderness programs, and correctional institutions"}, {"id": "b5de1b1c-2b2b-47c8-bf2d-e5ee6ba7a4b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Public and private facilities, licensing, accreditation, and oversight"}, {"id": "c8f165da-0eb7-44b9-b51b-7c219dc5d405", "type": "concept", "title": "Placement close to home and family contact"}], "description": "Students learn the range of out-of-home responses."}, {"id": "3103c182-6fad-4f79-9297-19e49594023c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conditions and rights", "children": [{"id": "7be2678a-d1de-4e71-becf-9c33f76adc45", "type": "concept", "title": "Education, special education, health care, mental health, substance use treatment, isolation, restraints, searches, and abuse prevention"}, {"id": "1f701216-c94c-47fe-a307-c8e60a21ee5c", "type": "concept", "title": "PREA, grievance systems, monitoring, and reporting"}, {"id": "f133fc88-591b-42cf-8426-280cc9faf422", "type": "concept", "title": "LGBTQ+ youth, girls, youth with disabilities, and pregnant/parenting youth"}], "description": "The point is to evaluate custody through safety and dignity."}, {"id": "a7655539-d386-4680-a4e6-da0201bd7381", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reentry and aftercare", "children": [{"id": "ae5a880e-6fe8-495b-80c0-3636d751d524", "type": "concept", "title": "Release planning, school re-enrollment, family support, housing, employment, mentoring, treatment continuity, and records relief"}, {"id": "b11358a6-3a28-481f-9e4d-19a853ce7a68", "type": "concept", "title": "Parole/aftercare supervision and technical violations"}, {"id": "1ada060c-1c1b-4831-9670-93b25c156820", "type": "concept", "title": "Community reintegration and desistance"}], "description": "Students connect confinement to return home."}]}, {"id": "5061e250-b894-407d-9751-5e51b3bff818", "type": "topic", "title": "Race, Ethnicity, Gender, Disability, LGBTQ+ Youth, and Disparities in Juvenile Justice", "description": "Students learn how unequal treatment and unequal conditions shape youth justice involvement, outcomes, legitimacy, and reform obligations.", "children": [{"id": "5d632fc2-4c41-4716-bfa7-d8bbb1ef15b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Racial and ethnic disparities", "children": [{"id": "a228fc65-d849-47fe-b538-9316b67bc1e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Police contact, school referral, detention, petition, adjudication, disposition, placement, transfer, and reentry"}, {"id": "436ec660-e46c-4d32-b5b4-01fafe84c58e", "type": "concept", "title": "OJJDP core requirement on racial and ethnic disparities"}, {"id": "2d11c52a-9cfd-45f3-ab7b-ad6ac731bcf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Data, benchmarks, and accountability"}], "description": "Students learn where disparities enter and compound."}, {"id": "22b92ec6-3443-46d7-afc6-fbfad32f1b8e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gender and identity", "children": [{"id": "1d08dc24-6160-4e9a-a3a8-22c5e63f5440", "type": "concept", "title": "Girls' pathways, survival behavior, trafficking, LGBTQ+ youth, gender expression, and sexual orientation"}, {"id": "732bfccd-ae89-4c23-85ef-56ec4e45b2e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Facility safety, classification, and services"}, {"id": "e72b0a31-8fed-4529-9208-6010863e37df", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed and affirming practice"}], "description": "The gist is to understand diverse youth pathways and needs."}, {"id": "69b853cf-6a8d-47ec-9189-43c5ecd11591", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Disability and language access", "children": [{"id": "f265d7c2-442c-425c-b14f-410c4f2bcd43", "type": "concept", "title": "IDEA, ADA, Section 504, special education, behavioral health, intellectual disability, autism, and language access"}, {"id": "832d53e3-da0e-4016-9abc-fda7de04f0e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Competency and comprehension"}, {"id": "db78941e-ed63-46c1-95dd-136035535387", "type": "concept", "title": "Accommodation and service coordination"}], "description": "Students learn legal and ethical duties to youth with disabilities."}]}, {"id": "483e1060-33fb-40fd-9aa8-ed0b666f2008", "type": "topic", "title": "Crossover Youth: Child Welfare, Behavioral Health, Substance Use, Schools, and Families", "description": "This topic focuses on young people moving across systems and the need for coordinated, trauma-informed, family-centered responses.", "children": [{"id": "bea7464a-d110-4466-a102-371997ba000e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cro